From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crewship <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(brief): add opt-in crew board instructions

Show peer coordination instructions and a read-only supervisor firehose
step only when the board socket exists. The socket is CREWBOARD_SOCKET, else
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/crewboard.sock, else /run/user/<uid>/crewboard.sock. Keep
the steering inbox, watcher, and durable status protocol unchanged.
---
 bin/fm-brief.sh                    | 15 +++++++++++++++
 bin/fm-supervision-instructions.sh |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bin/fm-brief.sh b/bin/fm-brief.sh
index 2ff9c727..539d55b3 100755
--- a/bin/fm-brief.sh
+++ b/bin/fm-brief.sh
@@ -366,6 +366,21 @@ if [ -e "$CONFIG/wait-no-turns" ]; then
   INBOX_SECTION+="Do not poll or list the inbox while waiting; a waiting instruction rings."$'\n'
 fi
 INBOX_SECTION=${INBOX_SECTION%$'\n'}
+BOARD_SOCK=${CREWBOARD_SOCKET:-${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$(id -u)}/crewboard.sock}
+if [ -S "$BOARD_SOCK" ]; then
+  IFS= read -r -d '' BOARD_SECTION <<EOF || true
+
+# Crew board
+The board permits direct peer coordination; report task states only to Firstmate through the status file.
+Use \`crewboard pub task/<peer-id> 'message'\` for a peer and \`crewboard pub fleet 'message'\` for the crew.
+Use \`crewboard pub fm 'message'\` for information that must not wake Firstmate.
+Read \`crewboard tail task/$ID\` and \`crewboard tail fleet\` at natural checkpoints, or subscribe in a separate pane.
+Use \`crewboard sub task/$ID fleet\` for that subscription; it waits for messages.
+Firstmate observes the board and never relays messages. The steering inbox remains unchanged.
+The board stores messages only in memory. Keep working, done, needs-decision, blocked, failed, and paused in the status file.
+EOF
+  INBOX_SECTION+=$'\n'"$BOARD_SECTION"
+fi
 
 # How a crewmate or scout waits. Every model turn resends the whole context, so
 # a wait must cost no turns: a decision wait ends the turn, and an external
diff --git a/bin/fm-supervision-instructions.sh b/bin/fm-supervision-instructions.sh
index 30e4fbde..4a4e08cb 100755
--- a/bin/fm-supervision-instructions.sh
+++ b/bin/fm-supervision-instructions.sh
@@ -271,6 +271,10 @@ fi
 if [ -n "$HOST_SNIPPET" ]; then
   printf '%s\n' '- Supervision host: on; it takes away-posture wakes and, where the dialog mirror is verified, eligible attended wakes itself, and hands the rest to you (protocol at the end of this block).'
 fi
+board_sock=${CREWBOARD_SOCKET:-${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/run/user/$(id -u)}/crewboard.sock}
+if [ -S "$board_sock" ]; then
+  printf '%s\n' "- Crew board: open a separate pane and run crewboard sub '*'; observe, never relay. The status file remains the durable ledger."
+fi
 ordinary_wake_line
 printf '\n'
 render_snippet
-- 
